s through partnerships and collaborations","section":"Item 1. Business","block":93,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001326732-26-000015","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-25","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001326732","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1326732/000132673226000015/xncr-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/f45a8f4cc4763bfbca6fe0f739ef36cced89b73e1a0d403fcddddff9513279a6.bin","sha256":"f45a8f4cc4763bfbca6fe0f739ef36cced89b73e1a0d403fcddddff9513279a6"}},{"id":"685668ee59ed2cd2cbe4c305e578cdbdaa3da59c33c55c75c586ab68afca201d","quote":"Generate revenue through licensing and collaboration arrangements","context":"We seek to utilize our protein engineering capabilities, XmAb Fc domains, XmAb multi-specific antibodies, and XmAb drug candidates in collaboration, licensing, and partnership arrangements to generate revenue while selectively retaining rights to advance certain prioritized programs internally, create new drug candidates, explore combination therapies, and identify additional indications for our pipeline programs.","section":"Item 1. Business","block":94,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001326732-26-000015","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-25","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001326732","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1326732/000132673226000015/xncr-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/f45a8f4cc4763bfbca6fe0f739ef36cced89b73e1a0d403fcddddff9513279a6.bin","sha256":"f45a8f4cc4763bfbca6fe0f739ef36cced89b73e1a0d403fcddddff9513279a6"}},{"id":"71f902b87c40d86c4241585fba6fdc2beda83efc7558d2e04c364a5d3e10049a","quote":"The modular nature of our Fc technologies and our ability to efficiently generate multiple drug candidates provide opportunities to generate revenue from licensing and collaboration agreements with third parties.","context":"Generate revenue through licensing and collaboration arrangements","section":"Item 1. Business","block":95,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001326732-26-000015","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-25","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001326732","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1326732/000132673226000015/xncr-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/f45a8f4cc4763bfbca6fe0f739ef36cced89b73e1a0d403fcddddff9513279a6.bin","sha256":"f45a8f4cc4763bfbca6fe0f739ef36cced89b73e1a0d403fcddddff9513279a6"}},{"id":"7a276df6fe9b13873a4d994cd73246db9d88cab1b66d41e164d2da47899dc16a","quote":"Create new XmAb drug candidates and evaluate combination therapies","context":"The modular nature of our Fc technologies and our ability to efficiently generate multiple drug candidates provide opportunities to generate revenue from licensing and collaboration agreements with third parties.","section":"Item 1. Business","block":96,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001326732-26-000015","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-25","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001326732","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1326732/000132673226000015/xncr-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/f45a8f4cc4763bfbca6fe0f739ef36cced89b73e1a0d403fcddddff9513279a6.bin","sha256":"f45a8f4cc4763bfbca6fe0f739ef36cced89b73e1a0d403fcddddff9513279a6"}},{"id":"eaaf9d6c8a001a40c3e145e091abd08169911af85e6b169dcd4002e9f20332c4","quote":"We aim to leverage our XmAb Fc domains and protein engineering technologies, independently and with partners, to create novel XmAb drug candidates and, where appropriate, to evaluate our candidates in combination with other therapeutic agents.","context":"Create new XmAb drug candidates and evaluate combination therapies","section":"Item 1. Business","block":97,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001326732-26-000015","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-25","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001326732","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1326732/000132673226000015/xncr-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/f45a8f4cc4763bfbca6fe0f739ef36cced89b73e1a0d403fcddddff9513279a6.bin","sha256":"f45a8f4cc4763bfbca6fe0f739ef36cced89b73e1a0d403fcddddff9513279a6"}},{"id":"451f43eac7b0b40c9329b70a219fa981503586db01e2801d9bee9dc05359e45b","quote":"Expand the functionality of XmAb technology platforms","context":"We aim to leverage our XmAb Fc domains and protein engineering technologies, independently and with partners, to create novel XmAb drug candidates and, where appropriate, to evaluate our candidates in combination with other therapeutic agents.","section":"Item 1. Business","block":98,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001326732-26-000015","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-25","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001326732","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1326732/000132673226000015/xncr-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/f45a8f4cc4763bfbca6fe0f739ef36cced89b73e1a0d403fcddddff9513279a6.bin","sha256":"f45a8f4cc4763bfbca6fe0f739ef36cced89b73e1a0d403fcddddff9513279a6"}},{"id":"5c1c745e75ff020888287ac3aa3532e804f6db9858aab4f0cac8042347245d93","quote":"We continue to conduct research into the function and application of multi-specific antibodies to broaden the scope of our XmAb technology platforms. Our modular designs allow us to engineer XmAb drug candidates across a range of structural formats and biological functions. We are engineering new molecular formats based on our Fc domains to develop novel molecules for engaging three targets simultaneously, called trispecific antibodies, to create highly specific cancer therapies, while overcoming the inherent structural and stability problems for standard trispecific molecules.","context":"Expand the functionality of XmAb technology platforms","section":"Item 1. Business","block":99,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001326732-26-000015","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-25","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001326732","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1326732/000132673226000015/xncr-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/f45a8f4cc4763bfbca6fe0f739ef36cced89b73e1a0d403fcddddff9513279a6.bin","sha256":"f45a8f4cc4763bfbca6fe0f739ef36cced89b73e1a0d403fcddddff9513279a6"}},{"id":"eaf60a21a6b80b247ef5d87575ca2a5077d4d984d2c0ede54c9bfaca6990335c","quote":"Protect and expand our intellectual property portfolio","context":"We continue to conduct research into the function and application of multi-specific antibodies to broaden the scope of our XmAb technology platforms. Our modular designs allow us to engineer XmAb drug candidates across a range of structural formats and biological functions. We are engineering new molecular formats based on our Fc domains to develop novel molecules for engaging three targets simultaneously, called trispecific antibodies, to create highly specific cancer therapies, while overcoming the inherent structural and stability problems for standard trispecific molecules.","section":"Item 1. Business","block":100,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001326732-26-000015","form":"10-K","filedAt":"2026-02-25","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001326732","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1326732/000132673226000015/xncr-20251231.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/f45a8f4cc4763bfbca6fe0f739ef36cced89b73e1a0d403fcddddff9513279a6.bin","sha256":"f45a8f4cc4763bfbca6fe0f739ef36cced89b73e1a0d403fcddddff9513279a6"}},{"id":"d144da55f3d86da3d0b0859cb393548dfc0a49a5573d9dce82b27ec0f9e0cf6d","quote"